### DenialFlow AI — example HTTP calls (VS Code REST Client)

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### Health-ish
GET {{base}}/docs

### Upload claims CSV (multipart)

Use `curl` or the Streamlit **Upload** page. REST multipart examples vary by client; prefer UI for demos.

### Start workflow (replace batch id)
POST {{base}}/v1/workflows/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "batch_id": "REPLACE_BATCH_ID",
  "max_claims": 3
}

### Workflow run + events
GET {{base}}/v1/workflows/REPLACE_RUN_ID
GET {{base}}/v1/workflows/REPLACE_RUN_ID/events

### Metrics
GET {{base}}/v1/metrics/dashboard
GET {{base}}/v1/metrics/ops

### Claims
GET {{base}}/v1/claims/summary?limit=50

### Appeals queue + detail + HITL
GET {{base}}/v1/appeals?limit=20
GET {{base}}/v1/appeals/REPLACE_APPEAL_ID

### Bedrock second opinion (analyzes CrewAI/Groq draft; requires AWS + BEDROCK_MODEL_REVIEW)
POST {{base}}/v1/appeals/REPLACE_APPEAL_ID/ai-review

POST {{base}}/v1/appeals/REPLACE_APPEAL_ID/approve

POST {{base}}/v1/appeals/REPLACE_APPEAL_ID/reject
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reason": "Insufficient documentation for payer policy section X." }

POST {{base}}/v1/appeals/REPLACE_APPEAL_ID/edit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "final_text": "Dear Payer,\n\nPlease reconsider...\n", "reason": "Legal tone adjustment" }
